critical_partition_consequence=for a pointwise cover at zero excess, m=1 a.e.; on each actual closed positive-length carrier component K, every pair intersection is relatively open and a nonempty one has positive length, so the relatively open owners are disjoint and clopen in connected K; one owner contains all of K; closed K inside an open D_w tooth gives ell<1/(7w); all owner bounds are <=6<15
critical_gram=for f_i=1_(D_wi)|C-1/7, an exact critical partition has Gram (h/49)(7I-J), rank 6, and sum_i f_i=0; near-critical deformations are delta_i=c_i-h/7 and p_ij=mu(C cap D_wi cap D_wj)
scope=top-seven compatibility scout and exact critical-boundary obstruction only; arbitrary seven-label packets remain open
all_exact_controls=PASS
